==Trivia==
*He is based on [[wikipedia:Beluga whale|beluga whales]], which are known for their echolocation abilities and lack of dorsal fins.
*The name Tappa may be derived from the Swedish word ''täppa'' (to block or obstruct a passage, pipe, drain or the like). It could also be a deliberately unfitting name derived from the Finnish words ''tappaa'' (to kill), ''tappaja'' (killer) or ''tappava'' (deadly), which would be ironic given Kid Tappa's low DPS.
*His Japanese name, Manabu-kun, is a reference to the work-and-hobby-focused magazine ''[[wikipedia:ja:ケイコとマナブ|Keiko to Manabu]]'', as proven by the line "His girlfriend Keiko said he should start looking for a real job" in his Japanese description.
**His joining the elite [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] shock division could be an allusion to ''Keiko to Manabu''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s publisher, [[wikipedia:ja:リクルートホールディングス|Recruit Holdings]].
*His behavior may refer to how real-life shock troops are expected to lead attacks and absorb heavy damage.

